            <div xml:id="d756">

                <pb facs="0703" n="691" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg691"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Stettinius Mission/64: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-26T22:00:00+02:00">April 26, 1944—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 26—9:27 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3443. Deles No. 34. From the Under Secretary. During their talks on Saudi Arabia
                    Sir Maurice Peterson and Murray agreed as to the desirability of accelerating
                    consideration of the Saudi Arabian financial <pb facs="0704" n="692"
                        xml:id="pg692"/> problem, and particularly of the proposals for the
                    establishment of a currency system, now under discussion between the Department
                    and the Treasury and the British Embassy.<anchor n="83" xml:id="d756-f1"/> Since
                    this is closely related to the question of a goods subsidy program and the
                    contemplated shipment of further supplies of silver from the United States,
                    which the British consider undesirable, I hope the Department can expedite
                    action on this subject in Washington. [Stettinius.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
